  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Solve for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi]$ given $\\cos 2\\theta+\\sin\\theta=1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\theta=0,\\ \\dfrac{\\pi}{6},\\ \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6},\\ \\pi,\\ 2\\pi$.\n\nUse $\\cos 2\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\theta$ and factorise.",
      "worked": "Using $\\cos 2\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\theta$,\n$$\\begin{align*}1-2\\sin^2\\theta+\\sin\\theta&=1\\\\-2\\sin^2\\theta+\\sin\\theta&=0\\\\\\sin\\theta(1-2\\sin\\theta)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\sin\\theta=0$ or $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac12$.\n\nOn $[0,2\\pi]$, $\\sin\\theta=0$ gives $\\theta=0,\\pi,2\\pi$, and $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac12$ gives $\\theta=\\dfrac\\pi6,\\dfrac{5\\pi}6$.\n\nTherefore $\\theta=0,\\dfrac\\pi6,\\dfrac{5\\pi}6,\\pi,2\\pi$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
